I've written the plan for this session (Day 254, 22:40): two task files and the issue responses. The commit step didn't happen because git ignores session_plan/. The files are on disk, which I'm assuming is where the harness reads them; I haven't checked that.

• Task 1: closes #1168 and the upstream #1164. This is @yuanhao's ticket, and the automatic yoagent 0.27.7 update stays rolled back until it lands. It follows his Do list as written: move the lock to 0.27.7, delete GOOGLE_PUBLISHED_LIMITS and its helper functions, and rewrite the two Gemini guards instead of deleting them. The new rule is that every Gemini model yoyo offers has a yoagent preset with real limits, not the 1,000,000 / 8192 guess. It also records the removed table as a superseded claim in ARCHITECTURE.md. This task touches 4 Rust files, one over the 3-file limit. It can't be split: the update turns the guards red, and deleting the table breaks the build, so neither half passes tests alone. The task file says this.
• Task 2: closes #1169, a bug the assessment reproduced with the built binary. When the first line of git status --porcelain starts with a space, the banner says "1 staged" and /git stage offers a path that has lost its first letter ("argo.toml"). The cause is that run_git / run_git_in_dir strip leading spaces from git's output. The task writes a failing test first in a temp repo. Then it checks the ~103 places that call those helpers before changing them to trim only trailing whitespace. If any caller relies on the leading trim, the fallback is to send only the status readers through a version that doesn't trim.

Both tasks close an issue, which brings the backlog down (13 listed, plus #1169). They also avoid context.rs and config.rs, which are 15 and 10 lines from failing the file-size check. #1167 is next in line. I skipped the long-thread issue review this session; #1012 (25 comments) is the next one to review. No release, since it isn't due (5 days, 50 commits).
